---
/**
 * The 404: the canonical small record (`DesignSystem-Pages.md` §3), and the
 * site's second plate page.
 *
 * One artifact, in the shape the document prints:
 *
 *   # ROUTE_404
 *   〈NOT FOUND〉
 *   /TRACE: [REQUESTED PATH]
 *   STATUS: INTERRUPTED
 *   SIGNAL: ABSENT / ROUTE: UNRESOLVED
 *   [one plain-language sentence]
 *   [the blank interval]
 *   LAND:
 *   ↳RETURN TO INDEX
 *   [ BACK TO LAND ]
 *
 * THE RECORD IS THE BLOCK LAYER'S, NOT THIS FILE'S. The page used to assemble
 * the two-panel record by hand - `FieldRecordDataCard`, `FieldRecordIndex`, a
 * hand-written `h1`, `FieldRecordStatus`, `FieldRecordEvidence` and a gutter
 * painted `var(--Background)` (invisible: the exact defect M1 fixed on the live
 * hero). That composition is `RecordHero`, which had no consumer at all; this
 * page is the third surface the artifact set allows it (homepage, release
 * summary, 404), so the page hands over a record and the block prints it.
 *
 * The evidence is a `RecordFigure`, not a bare plate: an uncaptioned figure is
 * decoration (`DESIGN-COMPLETE.md` §4.3), and a 404 has no evidence of its own -
 * which is exactly what its caption says, with the file it came from under it.
 *
 * ─── WHAT THIS CARD ADDS: THE TRACE PLATE ─────────────────────────────────
 * A 404 is the one page on the site whose whole subject is an absence, so it is
 * the one page that is honestly a PLATE. Under the record the page now prints
 * the thing that actually failed - the requested path - at full bleed, in a
 * `ShellPlate` with a caption channel that names it (`FIGURE:`), cites it
 * (`SOURCE: REQUEST URL`) and states it (`STATE: UNAVAILABLE`). The record says
 * `SIGNAL: ABSENT`; the plate shows *what* is absent. Neither decorates the
 * other: the record is the claim and the plate is its evidence.
 *
 * The plate's trace arm is the plate's own variant for a value rather than a
 * picture: the path prints at the L tier, wraps inside the field, and can never
 * widen the document. A path long enough to need more than one line also prints
 * the `too-long` state under it, which says what was clipped and where the limit
 * is - an adverse state composed in the same band, not a placeholder.
 *
 * Three decisions worth knowing before editing this file:
 *
 * - **The record is two panels, not a centred apology.** A data card beside an
 *   evidence fragment, a hairline gutter between them, `min-h-[80dvh]`: the
 *   composition HEAD rendered and the one `DESIGN.md` §3.5 names as the model
 *   for what "restored" means. The page caps the artifact's measure so a small
 *   record stays small; the block owns everything inside the cap.
 * - **The stamp is the page's only `h1`.** It renders `〈NOT FOUND〉` at the XL
 *   tier with the per-keyword ink the grammar gives a stamp's brackets and
 *   keyword (`RecordHero` prints the stamp through `StampText`). HEAD printed
 *   the same string as a `p`; a page with no `h1` has no document title, so the
 *   level-one heading is the fix, not a decoration.
 * - **`INTERRUPTED` is an ink state, not a quiet one.** `DesignSystem-Grammar.md`
 *   §2 fixes the tone per term: `INTERRUPTED` is ink (error, plain explanation +
 *   recovery), and `quiet` is reserved for `PREPARING` and `ARCHIVED`. The value
 *   carried `quiet`, which muted the one word that tells a reader what happened.
 *
 * The blank interval between the facts and the title block is mandatory
 * (`DesignSystem.md` INVARIANT 06, `DESIGN.md` §2.7): it is what gives `LAND:`
 * the weight of a second headline. Delete it and the record loses its shape.
 */
import { Header } from "../Component/Layout/Header";
import Onward from "../Component/More/Onward.astro";
import RecordFigure from "../Component/Record/RecordFigure.astro";
import RecordHero from "../Component/Record/RecordHero.astro";
import PageShell from "../Component/Shell/PageShell.astro";
import ShellPlate from "../Component/Shell/ShellPlate.astro";
import ShellState from "../Component/Shell/ShellState.astro";
import { NotFoundOnward, NotFoundOnwardCopy } from "../Content/More/Page.js";
import { NotFoundPage } from "../Content/Layout/NotFound.js";
import Base from "../Layout/Base.astro";
import { GetI18n } from "../Library/I18n/Server";

import type { Hero, LedgerRow } from "../Component/Record/Type.js";

const T = GetI18n();

const MetaTitle = T("common.error.404", {
	defaultValue: "404: No Record At This Address",
});

/**
 * The full error copy stays the document's description - all of it, including
 * the two sentences about checking the URL and opening an issue.
 */
const NotFoundCopy = T("common.error.pageNotFound", {
	defaultValue:
		"No record is filed at this address, and no redirect covers it. The address is well formed; nothing was ever filed under it.\n\n/Contents lists every route the build emits, so a link that used to work can be found there by name.\n\nIf a page of this site sent you here, /Contact takes the report and the path you came from.",
});

const MetaDescription = NotFoundCopy;

/**
 * The requested path the record's `TRACE:` line prints. The baseline printed
 * the route the reader asked for, so the line stays live rather than fixed.
 */
const RequestedPath = Astro.url.pathname;

/**
 * Whether the path will not print on the plate's one line. The plate wraps it
 * either way - this only decides whether the page also prints the state that
 * says so, which is the difference between a layout that survives a long value
 * and a page that acknowledges one.
 */
const IsLongPath = RequestedPath.length > 64;

/** The plate's and the states' copy, resolved from the route's own module. */
const Copy = NotFoundPage(T);

/**
 * The record. `claim` is the bare keyword - `StampText` draws the `〈 〉` - and
 * the two facts are ledger rows, which is what they are: the signal is absent and
 * the route is unresolved. The relation and the proposition sit below the blank
 * interval, where the interval gives them the weight of a second headline.
 */
const Record: Hero = {
	index: "ROUTE_404",
	claim: "NOT FOUND",
	route: `/TRACE:${RequestedPath}`,
	status: { state: "interrupted", tone: "ink" },
	seal: "Land",
	metadata: [
		{ key: "SIGNAL:", value: "ABSENT" },
		{ key: "ROUTE:", value: "UNRESOLVED" },
	] satisfies readonly LedgerRow[],
	relation: "LAND:",
	proposition: "RETURN TO INDEX",
	action: { label: "BACK TO LAND", href: "/", variant: "button" },
};
---

<Base Title={MetaTitle} Description={MetaDescription} noIndex={true}>
	<Header client:load slot="Header" />

	<PageShell index="# PLATE_01" label="THE MISSING RECORD">
		<RecordHero {...Record} slot="head">
			<RecordFigure
				src="/Evidence/Land/NightGlass-01.png"
				alt="Rain-speckled glass reflecting a green light at night"
				caption="A 404 has no evidence of its own, so the record prints the site's plate."
				provenance="/EVIDENCE/LAND/NIGHTGLASS-01.PNG"
			/>
		</RecordHero>

		<ShellPlate
			index="01"
			figure={Copy.plate.figure}
			source={Copy.plate.source}
			state={Copy.plate.state}
			proposition={Copy.plate.proposition}
			trace={{
				mark: Copy.plate.mark,
				value: RequestedPath,
				note: Copy.plate.note,
			}}
			bleed="viewport"
			height="clamp(15rem, 32vh, 24rem)"
		/>

		{
			IsLongPath ? (
				<ShellState
					kind="too-long"
					index="TRACE / 01"
					value={RequestedPath}
					limit={Copy.tooLong.limit}
					statement={Copy.tooLong.statement}
					cause={Copy.tooLong.cause}
					next={Copy.tooLong.next}
					note={`CHARACTERS: ${RequestedPath.length}\u2001LIMIT: ${Copy.tooLong.limit}`}
				/>
			) : null
		}

		<ShellState
			kind="missing"
			index="RECORD / 01"
			statement={Copy.missing.statement}
			cause={Copy.missing.cause}
			next={Copy.missing.next}
			rows={[
				{ key: "WAS:", value: RequestedPath, code: true },
				{ key: "TARGET:", value: "UNRESOLVED" },
				{ key: "SIGNAL:", value: "ABSENT" },
			]}
			note={"SOURCE: REQUEST URL\u2001FILED: NEVER"}
		/>

		{/*
			The way out. The page used to tell the reader that `/Contents` lists
			every route the build emits and then not link it - an apology with no
			handle on it. `Onward` is the routing register: six intents, in the
			order a reader who typed a wrong address is likely to have meant them,
			and the first is the index the copy above already names.

			It is a `<nav>` and not a section: a page that has just said "no record
			at this address" does not need a heading to introduce its exits, and a
			heading would make the way out a subject of its own.
		*/}
		<Onward rows={NotFoundOnward} copy={NotFoundOnwardCopy} />
	</PageShell>
</Base>
